{title: The Old Rugged Cross}
{key: D}

{comment: Verse 1}
On a [A]hill far away stood an [Dmaj7]old rugged cross
The [E7]emblem of suffering and [A]shame
And I [A]love that old cross where the [Dmaj7]dearest and best
For a [E7]world of lost [A]sinners was slain

{comment: Chorus}
I will [E]cherish the old rugged [A]cross
'Til my [D]trophies at last I lay [A]down
I will [A]cling to the [A7]old rugged [D]cross[Dm]
And ex[A]change it some[E]day for a [A]crown

{comment: Verse 2}
Oh, that [A]old rugged cross, so des[Dmaj7]pised by the world,
Has a [E7]wondrous attraction for [A]me;
For the [A]dear Lamb of God left His [Dmaj7]glory above
To [E7]bear it to dark Cal[A]vary.

{comment: Verse 3}
To the [A]old rugged cross I will [Dmaj7]ever be true
Its [E7]shame and reproach gladly [A]bear
'Til He [A]calls me some day to my [Dmaj7]home far away
Where His [E7]glory forever I'll [A]share
